A1. A famous bird of paradox. ~ SHAW
A5. This makes a gay old dog show his teeth. ~ SMILE
A10. What the prodigal son did on the primrose path. ~ TROD
A14. That ticklish sensation you can't scratch. ~ LOVE
A15. A wise cracker can get this. ~ PECAN
A16. Some women are all wrapped up in this. ~ ROBE
A17. This hasn't a leg to stand on. ~ APOD
A18. You've got to be this to avoid stowaways. ~ ALERT
A19. Drug-giving plant. ~ ALOE
A20. This is always in suspense. ~ PENDANT
A22. How you'll find picnic grounds in the Catskills ~ DEFILED
A24. Irritate. ~ IRK
A25. Denizen of the underworld. ~ RAT
A26. It's still legal to do this with your eyes. ~ DRINK
A29. You'll find this on the end of a camel. ~ ASH
A32. The old Indian sign. ~ TOTEM
A36. If you slip on this it may ruin you for life. ~ RING
A37. A well-known fumbler. ~ PIKER
A39. Do this and you'll lose your head. ~ RAVE
A40. If you see red don't cross this (abbr.). ~ AVE
A41. This used to cross the bar in schooners. ~ MARINER
A43. This has whiskers on it. ~ CAT
A44. A big get-together. ~ MERGER
A46. To run down. ~ DERIDE
A48. Flower extract. ~ ATTAR
A49. You can take a couple of these and beat it. ~ TOM
A52. Pretty hard to crash this gatekeeper. ~ PETER
A53. What was Prometheus Unbound? ~ LIBERATED
A56. What John Roach Straton expects us to do in the hereafter. ~ SWELTER
A59. Chooses. ~ SELECTS
A63. What an ambitious Italian works for. ~ LIRA
A64. This could set the world on fire. ~ ARSON
A66. A very large basin. ~ ERIE
A67. He's written more stuff than any other author. ~ ANON
A68. There's nothing square about this kind of thing. ~ ROUND
A69. It's stylish to follow this. ~ MODE
A70. You can't better this. ~ BEST
A71. Fine feathers. ~ DRESS
A72. What Major Seagrave did on the road to fame. ~ SPED

D1. A fancy sock. ~ SLAP
D2. Lose this and you're lost. ~ HOPE
D3. Bill Shakespeare's swimming hole. ~ AVON
D4. The end of a love affair. ~ WEDDING
D5. What the older generation would like to do to the younger generation. ~ SPANK
D6. What bankrolls do at nightclubs. ~ MELT
D7. What the iceman told the maid about. ~ ICE
D8. This is fat. ~ LARD
D9. You'll be an outsider if you don't do this. ~ ENTER
D10. This kind of person just couldn't be true. ~ TRAITOR
D11. What the dunkin' sisters have for breakfast. ~ ROLL
D12. A windy instrument. ~ OBOE
D13. If the Boy Scouts do this it's supposed to be good. ~ DEED
D21. What a beastly place this was. ~ ARK
D23. A hoggish corporation. ~ FAT
D26. People are always acting up in this. ~ DRAMA
D27. An overgrown nail. ~ RIVET
D28. You're usually lying if you say you're this. ~ INERT
D29. A good thing to give a windy young man. ~ AIR
D30. A winter slipper. ~ SKI
D31. This is always laying around the place. ~ HEN
D33. Silent. ~ TACIT
D34. What we'd like to do to a bill collector. ~ EVADE
D35. Keep your eye on this if you go for a ride. ~ METER
D37. You'll usually find Walter Hagen under this. ~ PAR
D38. You'll get this in the face if you get angry. ~ RED
D41. Just desert. ~ MERIT
D42. Thrust back. ~ REPEL
D45. Ye old-fashioned handkisser. ~ GALLANT
D47. Unhocks. ~ REDEEMS
D49. What Emily Post would feel if she met a lion. ~ TERROR
D50. Either's l'il pal. ~ OR
D51. A higher order of mammals that lays bricks (pl.). ~ MASONS
D54. This covers a multitude of chins. ~ BEARD
D55. What a sheepherder does. ~ TENDS
D56. A cold bed at the morgue. ~ SLAB
D57. The first of a famous trio. ~ WINE
D58. Aphrodite's little boy. ~ EROS
